A||N||5||Haze_Performance||Heater Core hose question?||||7||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||09-20-2001||12:39 AM||||Earlier this year me heater core started to leak. I put it a new one a month ago. Now I have antifreeze on my passengers side carpet AGAIN. There's no water/antifreeze under the hood. (Front) Maybe one of the the rubber hoses are leaking now? Are the hoses molded or can I buy a length of hose & replace them? I went to the auto parts store today & they told me all they have is "cut your own" hose. Any info will be appreciated. <P><BR>Thank You <BR>-Haze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">    .    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">    .    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole_6_2.gif">        <BR><I><B><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners</B></I></FONT> - <FONT COLOR="red"><A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A></FONT>||||reg||7
Z||000001||SLYGUY||09-20-2001||02:45 AM||||If there is antifreeze on your floor and you've replaced that heater core it can only be the hose. <P>I'd drain the radiator, disconnect the hose at the rad and the heater core and take a good look at it. Probably a pin hole leak. <P>Having it in your hands will help in assuring that you get the right diameter and length at the auto parts store. <BR>I was able to get the right radiator hoses for a truck I have. Maybe they have the right diameter, length, and bend hoses to fit your car. <BR>Take the hose out and take it with you to get a good match.<P>Good luck,<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||09-20-2001||09:39 AM||||Well, the heater pipe to heater core hoses (the 2 hoses up front that connect to the heater core) are moulded hose with 90* bends at the heater core.  The Fiero Store sells replacements for about $9-10 each, but they only fit non-ac cars.  Since I'm getting ready to replace the heater core on my 88 Formula with A/C, I'm looking for alternatives, too.  The bend is too tight for straight hose, unless you do a big loop of hose, and that would be ridiculous.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Phil||09-20-2001||09:51 AM||||I used the Fiero Store hoses of my wife's 88 coupe with AC- I  cut the hose just below where it passes thru the spare tire compartment floor and added an extension made out of some copper tubing. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||09-20-2001||01:31 PM||||Hey man gimme your address and I'll send you a hose, 10 bucks gets you a heater core hose and shipping  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000005||theogre||09-20-2001||08:10 PM||||pull the cover off and look... It wouln't be the first time a replacement core let go.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
